    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1: Number of hectares of biological significant areas showing improved biophysical conditions  (M&amp;E plan)
2: Number of Institutions with improved capacity to address sustainable landscape issues as supported by USG assistance (M&amp;E plan)
3: Number of people (dis-aggregated by men &amp; women) receiving livelihood co-benefits (monetary or non-monetary) associated with the implementation of USG sustainable landscapes activities (M&amp;E plan)
4: Area under sustainable forest management (hectares) (M&amp;E plan)
5: Number of community groups that are participating in decision-making process at union and above level. (M&amp;E plan)
6: Number of new groups or initiatives created through USG funding dedicated to resolving the conflict or the
drivers of conflict (M&amp;E plan)
7: Number of laws, policies, regulation or standards Addressing sustainable landscapes formally proposed,
adapted or implemented as supported by USG assistance(M&amp;E plan).
8: Number of hectares (seedlings) in all other areas under improved NRM, safeguards or sustainable practices
(M&amp;E plan)
9: Number of people trained in sustainable landscapes supported by USG assistance (M&amp;E plan).
10: Number of people trained in the project management and finance related issues supported by USG assistance (Project)
11: Number of people reached by a USG funded intervention providing GBV services(M&amp;E plan).
12: Percentage of female participants in USG-assisted programs designed to increase access to productive economic resources (assets, credit, income or employment).</narrative>
    </description>
